# ERROR-SURFACE PROBE (receipt E2b). Not an idiom.
#
# The SAME reserved word as reserved_word_bare.dl6, but its argument here parses
# as a rel atom, which is the shape registry.pl declares for subscribe/1
# (wrapper(rel_atom, refuse(lifecycle))). That reaches the good path:
#
#   refusal: unsupported_construct(lifecycle_arm(subscribe))
#
# named, precise, actionable. So the quality of the diagnostic depends on the
# SHAPE OF THE ARGUMENT rather than on the mistake: the author who deliberately
# writes a lifecycle arm is told exactly what is wrong, and the author who
# merely picked a reserved name for their own rel gets the char-code dump.
#
rel joined(reader: text)           log keep(all).
rel read_at(reader: text, at: int) key(1).

read_at(Reader, 0) <+ subscribe(joined(Reader)).
